$('#b-help').onclick=()=>dlg('Amni-CAD',[h('p',null,'Parametric CAD that runs entirely in your browser. Geometry is built by OpenCascade (an open-source geometry kernel) compiled to WebAssembly, so exports are exact solids. There is no account and no telemetry, and your designs stay on this device unless you turn on an optional online feature: a cloud AI provider with your own key, the Claude phone link, a vault server, or the on-device AI, which downloads its runtime from cdn.jsdelivr.net and its model from huggingface.co on first use. The privacy page lists exactly what each one sends.'),h('ul',null,h('li',null,'Add features on the left. Each one edits the solid in order; change any value and everything after it updates.'),h('li',null,'New parts start in inches (pick millimeters in New part). Results show imperial units first with metric in parentheses; the Units card on the Part panel converts a part or switches to metric first.'),h('li',null,'Form (top bar) is the organic workspace: blend shapes, sculpt with brushes, add bones and keyframes, and export animated glTF. The scene is plain text the AI edits line by line; Space plays the animation and [ ] resize the brush.'),h('li',null,'Any number can be an expression of parameters, such as w/2 - 8 or 2*t + 1. Trig functions take degrees.'),h('li',null,'Click faces and edges to measure them, then use them in fillets, holes, shells, sketch planes and stress tests.'),h('li',null,'Open the sketcher from any profile to draw lines, arcs and circles with dimensions and relations. Blue geometry can still move; black is fully defined. Dimensions can use your parameters.'),h('li',null,'Drag the orange rollback bar in the feature list to build only the features above it; new features are inserted there. Drag features to reorder them.'),h('li',null,'On phones and tablets, one finger orbits, two fingers pan and pinch zooms, a double tap fits the part and a long press opens the menu for what is under your finger (or explains a button). Panels slide up from the bottom: drag the handle to resize them or swipe down to close. In the sketcher, slide your finger to aim with the loupe and lift to place a point; dimensions accept units such as 2in or 50mm.'),h('li',null,'Interface switches between the Workshop and Blueprint layouts, each with a ribbon, feature tree, properties panel, middle-mouse orbit and standard view shortcuts.'),h('li',null,'The AI tab works with Claude, OpenAI, Gemini or OpenRouter (your key or sign-in), your Claude or ChatGPT subscription through the local bridge, an on-device model, or Ollama and LM Studio.'),h('li',null,'References in the AI tab hold your sketches, photos and PDF drawings (upload, take a photo, drop or paste). Add a note such as "top view, units inches" and press Model from references. They are saved with the design and sent only to the AI engine you pick.'),h('li',null,'Stress, Flow, Drawing and Review run on your device: stress and vibration on a voxel mesh, wind or water tunnels with lattice Boltzmann, internal flow through channels and porous layers (2.5D whole plate or 3D detail), automatic drawings with tolerances, and printability, wall thickness, mass and cost checks.')),h('p',null,h('b',null,'Shortcuts: '),h('kbd',null,'Ctrl Z'),' undo · ',h('kbd',null,'Ctrl Shift Z'),' redo · ',h('kbd',null,'F'),' fit · ',h('kbd',null,'0'),' iso · ',h('kbd',null,'1'),' top · ',h('kbd',null,'2'),' front · ',h('kbd',null,'3'),' right · ',h('kbd',null,'Del'),' delete feature · ',h('kbd',null,'Esc'),' clear selection'),h('p',null,h('b',null,'Workshop: '),h('kbd',null,'Ctrl 1…8'),' standard views · ',h('kbd',null,'Space'),' orientation · ',h('kbd',null,'Ctrl B'),' rebuild · middle-drag orbit, Ctrl pan, Shift zoom. ',h('b',null,'Blueprint: '),h('kbd',null,'Ctrl D'),' isometric view · ',h('kbd',null,'Ctrl G'),' regenerate · middle-drag orbit, Shift pan, Ctrl zoom. ',h('b',null,'Sketcher: '),h('kbd',null,'L'),' line · ',h('kbd',null,'R'),' rectangle · ',h('kbd',null,'C'),' circle · ',h('kbd',null,'A'),' arc · ',h('kbd',null,'D'),' dimension · ',h('kbd',null,'S'),' select · ',h('kbd',null,'F'),' fit.'),h('p',{class:'mut'},'Open-source pieces: OpenCascade via replicad (LGPL-2.1), three.js (MIT), pdf.js (Apache-2.0). Licenses are in /cad/vendor/.')]);
